{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetEqChimney","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetEqChimney","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetFromVertices","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronRegion"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.idealTet_eq_chimney","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.idealTet_eq_chimney","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetEqChimney.lean#L157-L191","doc":"**THE THEOREM.**  The Milnor-normalized ideal tetrahedron with far vertex `∞` and\nthree finite vertices on the unit circle at angles `t`, `t + 2γ`, `t + 2γ + 2α`\n(defined from those vertices in File A2, independently of any chord data) EQUALS the\nchimney over the inscribed triangle of angles `(α, β, γ)`.\n\nThis replaces `region_eq_chimney := rfl` with a genuine set-equality: the region is\nnow an independent object, and its coincidence with the chimney is a proved theorem,\nnot an adopted convention.  Sorry-free; the only cited input is the totally-geodesic\nclassification adopted as a definition in File A1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.face3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.face3","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetEqChimney.lean#L122-L153","doc":"**Face opposite `P₂`** (through `∞, P₁, P₃`), oriented toward `P₂`, projects to\nchord 3 of the inscribed triangle.  Here the half-angle `γ + α = π − β` exceeds\n`π/2`, so the signed area appears with the OPPOSITE sign; the orientation vertex\n`P₂` (negative side) still pins the half-space to chord 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.sareaP1P3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.sareaP1P3","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetEqChimney.lean#L100-L120","doc":"**The chord `P₁P₃` in chord-3 form.**  Its subtended half-angle `γ + α = π − β`\nexceeds `π/2`, so `sarea_circlePoint_unit` produces the perpendicular-bisector\ndirection `t + γ + α`, which is `θ₃ − π` for the chord-3 direction `θ₃ = t+2γ+2α+β`.\nRewriting with `α + β + γ = π` gives `sarea P₁P₃ w = 2 sin β · (w·nθ₃ − cos β)` —\nthe same functional chord 3 tests, up to the sign carried by the `− π` shift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.face2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.face2","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetEqChimney.lean#L73-L98","doc":"**Face opposite `P₁`** (through `∞, P₂, P₃`), oriented toward `P₁`, projects to\nchord 2 of the inscribed triangle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.face1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.face1","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetEqChimney.lean#L46-L71","doc":"**Face opposite `P₃`** (through `∞, P₁, P₂`), oriented toward `P₃`, projects to\nchord 1 of the inscribed triangle. ","signatureChunk":0}]}